# Stage 4 near layer (factor 13/16, factor_y 8/16, bottom-aligned at the
# level bottom): the Falkenstein's wooded slope. A j forest floor from row ~86
# down (opaque, so the mid layer's lake band never shows a sky gap as the
# layers sink at different speeds: rows >= 84 are opaque everywhere),
# spruces (G lit / j shade) along a treeline reaching up to row ~32, a lower
# row of spruces and larches (g lit / G shade) in front, four pale limestone
# outcrops (m body, i lit left facets, m strata, no lip) rising out of the
# trees, and a rockfall net (m mesh, d ropes) strung between two d/m posts
# beside the big outcrop. Near-layer colours, no k, no outlines. 180 px high
# is enough: the layer only ever moves down (D-054), so the sky behind it
# never gaps, and with factor_y 8 it has sunk 232 px (> 180) at the summit.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
# Tiles horizontally (640 px).
sprite = bg_falkenstein
size   = 640x180
origin = 0,0
anim   = idle frames=1
---
frame idle 0
